    <innerclass refid="classPasswordCrypt" prot="public">PasswordCrypt</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>A small wrapper around libsodium&apos;s password-hashing functions. (Originally: &quot;Thin wrapper around libsodium&apos;s password-hashing
primitives used by the password workers.&quot;). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header declares a class that turns a plain-text password into a stored hash, and that checks a plain-text password against a stored hash. New hashes use the Argon2id recipe, but older scrypt hashes are still understood so existing accounts keep working. The class holds almost no data of its own; its main job is to make sure libsodium is ready before any hashing happens.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: Checking passwords is the first line of defence for every login. The session manager calls <ref refid="classPasswordCrypt" kindref="compound">PasswordCrypt</ref> (through <ref refid="classPasswordWorker" kindref="compound">PasswordWorker</ref>) to verify passwords off the web request threads. Without this file there would be no safe way to store or check passwords, so nobody could log in to Valhalla.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Password hashing (Argon2/scrypt): <ulink url="https://doc.libsodium.org/password_hashing/">https://doc.libsodium.org/password_hashing/</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>OWASP password storage advice: <ulink url="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Password_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html">https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Password_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::optional (a value that may be missing): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Threads and concurrency in C++: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
